  <prompt>
    Make review findings durable-by-disposition. (a) Flip the agreement-review Binding's sprk_disposition
    informational→compose (Dataverse data — server code unchanged: the compose leg is already store-then-pass-through).
    (b) Extend ComposeWorkspace.materializeComposeDraftFromLedger with a FINDINGS branch: a compose-disposition payload
    carrying flaggedSections[] re-materializes via ComposeEditor.placeAdvisoryComments — preserving
    riskLevel/sectionRef/standardRef/flaggedClause/assessment — instead of falling into the draft/edits branches.
    Result: reopening a reviewed document restores the gutter Review Notes deterministically, zero LLM calls.
  </prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. ADR-040 ledger semantics, Compose materialization pipeline, Binding catalog data.</role>
  <goal>Reviews route through the durable compose path; reload re-materializes advisory comments with full metadata; no re-dispatch.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Verified seam (HUB-R1-REVIEW §4): OutputRouter writes SessionOutput with the Binding's disposition
      (OutputRouter.cs:193-224); compose leg = store-then-pass-through (:280-281) identical to informational — flipping
      the Binding row changes durability class without server code. GET /sessions/{id}/compose-outputs projects
      compose-disposition entries (ChatEndpoints.cs:1312-1334; skips truncation markers :1326-1329). The FR-04
      refresh-durability effect (ComposeWorkspace.tsx:1609-1616 → materializeComposeDraftFromLedger :1385-1484) branches
      on payload shape: edits[] / single-edit / comments[{target_text,comment}] / rationale. flaggedSections[] matches
      NO branch — add the findings branch calling placeAdvisoryComments (which carries metadata; the comments[]→
      registerAiReviewComments path would DROP risk/section/standard metadata — do not use it for findings).
      AUDIT-BEFORE-IMPLEMENT (nda-r1 lesson): re-verify these line refs and check nothing already routes findings.
      COORDINATION: spaarke-notification-spine-r1 flips the same DispositionRoutability registry surface (ADR-043) —
      /conflict-check before the PR. Session-routing (DEF-09) + apply-leg gating are task 031 — this task lands the
      branch + flip; 031 makes the write/read sessions coincide.
    </background>
